{
    "//": [
        "Manifest driving the document-type regression suite (tests/regression/).",
        "One representative blueprint per infra/document-types/ category today.",
        "Known coverage gaps: only one blueprint per category is tested (not the",
        "full blueprint matrix), and there are no negative/adversarial documents.",
        "",
        "Each case simulates a canned Bedrock Data Automation (BDA) result for the",
        "given blueprint/category and asserts our pipeline's classification,",
        "extraction-rule, and response-code behavior against it end to end (mocked",
        "AWS via moto; BDA itself cannot be moto-mocked, so its output is canned).",
        "",
        "document_class and fields (names, nesting, types) are taken from",
        "documentai_api/config/blueprint_schemas.json (the preloaded, real BDA",
        "blueprint schemas - see `make pull-blueprint-schemas`), not invented, so",
        "the suite exercises the actual field shape BDA returns for each blueprint,",
        "including nested/table fields (e.g. recipient_name.first_name) and",
        "non-string types (e.g. payment_amount as a number).",
        "",
        "'fields' simulates the explainability_info BDA would return: a leaf is",
        "{value, confidence[, type]}; anything else is a nested object and is",
        "recursed into (see conftest.py::build_explainability_info). value \"\"",
        "means BDA returned the field but with an empty value (as opposed to",
        "omitting it). 'required_fields'/'optional_fields' use the same dotted",
        "leaf names as the extracted field names (e.g. \"recipient_name.first_name\")",
        "and are seeded into the extraction-rules table for the tenant before the",
        "case runs. 'expected_missing_required_fields' is what the resulting DDB",
        "record's missingRequiredFieldList should contain."
    ],
    "cases": [
